  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Raj Prakash @ Neeraj vs State Of U.P. And 2 Others on 13 February, 2025 Author: Saurabh Srivastava Bench: Saurabh Srivastava High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Neutral Citation No. - 2025:Ahc:20481 Court No. - 79 Case :- Matters Under Article 227 No. - 16071 of 2024 Petitioner :- Raj Prakash @ Neeraj Respondent :- State Of U.P. And 2 Others",
    "facts": "Being aggrieved with order dated 26.7.2023, petitioner preferred a Criminal Appeal no. 135 of 2023 under Section 392 Cr.P.C. before court concerned but the same was rejected vide order dated 1.5.2024 passed by learned District and Sessions Judge, Firozabad which has been challenged through the instant petition.",
    "arguments": "(ii) to issue a writ, order or direction in the nature of commanding directing the respondent no. 2 and 3 not to take any coercive action against the petitioner in pursuance of the order dated 26.7.2023.\" 3. It is the case of petitioner that a complaint case no. 1102 of 2019 was filed by respondent no. 3 under section 51 of Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006 alleging therein that substandard milk samples were found in the dairy owned by petitioner. 4. It is contended by learned counsel for petitioner that order dated 26.07.2023 has been passed without giving any opportunity to the petitioner, hence the same is liable to be [LEAKAGE_MASK]. 5. Learned AGA vehemently opposed the prayer as made in the petition and rebutted the stand taken up by learned counsel for the petitioner and submitted that in spite of giving several opportunities, the same were failed to be availed by the petitioner.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. It is contended by learned counsel for petitioner that order dated 26.07.2023 has been passed without giving any opportunity to the petitioner, hence the same is liable to be [LEAKAGE_MASK]. 5. Learned AGA vehemently opposed the prayer as made in the petition and rebutted the stand taken up by learned counsel for the petitioner and submitted that in spite of giving several opportunities, the same were failed to be availed by the petitioner.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "(ii) to issue a writ, order or direction in the nature of commanding directing the respondent no. 2 and 3 not to take any coercive action against the petitioner in pursuance of the order dated 26.7.2023.\" 3. It is the case of petitioner that a complaint case no. 1102 of 2019 was filed by respondent no. 3 under section 51 of Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006 alleging therein that substandard milk samples were found in the dairy owned by petitioner."
